    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0094" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4231/939</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-19">January 19, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Canadian Minister called ostensibly to convey a message of greeting from the
                    Prime Minister of Canada.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d18-f1"/> He proceeded to say
                    that an announcement of the proposed trade agreement negotiations between his
                    Government and this Government would be made on Monday next, and that it might
                    or might not be necessary to make public the correspondence between the two
                    governments on this question, in view of the political or other exigencies. He
                    then said that, speaking entirely apart from official or other considerations,
                    the new trade proposal of the Prime Minister, along with certain other new
                    proposals, was greatly and favorably affecting public opinion back in the
                    direction of the Prime Minister and his Government.</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
                <pb facs="0095" n="19" xml:id="pg19"/>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of public notice issued by the Department of State, January 21,
                        1935, and statistics regarding the trade of the United States and Canada,
                        see Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>,
                        January 26, 1935, pages 44 ff.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d18-f1" n="4" xml:id="d18-f1-content">
                <p>R. B. Bennett, Canadian Prime Minister and Secretary of State for External
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
